# Source: https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/1053
# Symptom: chromosome name field is extremely long (hundreds of characters,
#   e.g. a composite reference ID joining dozens of accessions with "|");
#   bedtools merge truncates the name and emits garbled coordinate output.
#   While the BED spec does not impose a length limit on chrom names, this
#   pattern arises from poorly formatted composite reference identifiers and
#   causes silent data corruption in tools that use fixed internal buffers.
